    { math: '3 · Dating: relative and absolute', note: 'Radiocarbon (organic material to ~50 kya — Nobel 1960), thermoluminescence (fired objects), dendrochronology (tree rings — exact years), potassium-argon (volcanic, millions of years). Each material has its clock; multiple methods cross-check.' },
    { math: '4 · Reading a society from its stuff', note: 'Garbage tells truth (garbology is real); bones carry diet, disease, violence, workload (bioarchaeology); buildings encode power; distribution maps show trade and territory. Archaeology reconstructs societies from what they dropped.' },
  ],
};

