        'Because looting damages the artefact',
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'A pot in a museum can be beautiful and nearly useless; the same pot, recorded in situ, dates its layer, its use, its trade route and its household. The information lives in the relationships — and relationships are exactly what the looter destroys.',
