      choices: [
        'The equipment cannot measure older samples of any kind',
        'Carbon-14 decays with a 5,730-year half-life; by ~50,000 years too few atoms remain to measure reliably',
        'Carbon-14 is created only by human activity',
        'Older samples contain no carbon',
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'After about nine half-lives, the residual carbon-14 signal sinks into background noise. Older timescales switch clocks: uranium-series on cave carbonates, potassium-argon on volcanic layers, and — the precision instrument — dendrochronology back ~12,000 years.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Why did the Göbekli Tepe discovery (monumental enclosures ~9600 BCE) matter so much?',
